<article class="env-lemma" id="06CY">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06CY">Lemma <span data-tag="06CY">97.5.4</span>.</a> Let $p : \mathcal{X} \to \mathcal{Y}$ be a $1$-morphism of categories fibred in groupoids over $(\mathit{Sch}/S)_{fppf}$. Assume $p$ is representable by algebraic spaces and an open immersion. Then $p$ is limit preserving on objects. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/06CX" data-tag="06CX">97.5.3</a> and (via the general principle Algebraic Stacks, Lemma <a href="/tag/045F" data-tag="045F">94.10.9</a>) from the fact that an open immersion of algebraic spaces is locally of finite presentation, see Morphisms of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/06CN" data-tag="06CN">67.28.11</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>